description:
Part of #430. Branch `claude/fuzz-upload-retry-model` exists (empty, at origin/master).

Target: `uploadTransactionsWithFallback` (src/services/powersync.ts, exported as `__uploadTransactionsWithFallbackForTest`). The existing powersync.fuzz.test.ts covers only compactBlockCrudEntries/orderedBlockUpserts — not this orchestrator, which has been broken and re-fixed at least SIX times (2b18b676c missing-row RPC rollback, 58140b90d per-tx rejection tolerance, 71bd72efe HTTP-status threading so permanent 4xx don't jam the queue, 267558e29 atomic+idempotent rejection recording, 9fc1b8729 oversized-batch cap, 05fe86074 succeeded-prefix drain killing re-touch amplification).

Harness: drive with N generated transactions and an injected upload fn whose per-attempt outcomes come from a generated script (success / transient / permanent-4xx / ambiguous, mirroring the REAL error shapes the classifier switches on). Track all observable side effects. Properties:
(a) every tx reaches exactly ONE terminal fate (completed-success / completed-with-recorded-rejection / still-pending) — never double-completed, never silently dropped;
(b) a succeeded prefix is never re-uploaded after a later transient failure;
(c) permanent failures never jam the queue — remaining txs still attempted;
(d) ambiguous outcomes never exceed the retry budget before quarantine;
(e) rejection recording idempotent.
Pin the REAL contract where the sketch and code disagree; this is live sync code — report rather than "fix" anything ambiguous.

Part of #430. Remainder of the guard/classifier pack whose first slice landed as PR #429. Branch `claude/fuzz-guard-classifiers` exists with that slice.

**1. `src/utils/test/localDbCorruption.fuzz.test.ts`** — `isLocalDbCorruptionError`, `isRuntimeDbCorruptionError`, `messageChainOf`, `toLocalDbOpenError` (src/utils/localDbCorruption.ts; all pure). These classifiers route users toward a DESTRUCTIVE recovery UI, so false positives are dangerous (see the never-auto-wipe policy). Properties:
- totality: never throws for arbitrary error shapes — Error with deep `.cause` chains, worker-boundary plain objects, primitives, null/undefined, and a manufactured **cyclic** `.cause` (messageChainOf's depth≤5 bound must terminate);
- monotonicity: `isRuntimeDbCorruptionError(e)` ⟹ `isLocalDbCorruptionError(e)` (RUNTIME_CORRUPTION_SUBSTRINGS ⊆ CORRUPTION_SUBSTRINGS);
- bare `'malformed'` embedded in random text, without the exact SQLite phrases ('disk image is malformed' / 'malformed database schema'), must never match;
- `toLocalDbOpenError` idempotent on an already-wrapped error.
Evidence: 6e8136fe0 (worker-boundary plain objects), 1678637cb (tight runtime matcher), issue #284 / iPad OPFS incidents.

**2. `packages/agent-cli/test/subtreeOutline.fuzz.test.ts`** — `renderSubtreeOutline` / `collapseVerticalMotion`. Anti-spoofing invariant (one line per block, id-first) broken twice by missed vertical-motion character classes (34a586e92 Unicode line separators, 8fcfafe42 C0 information separators). Properties over arbitrary rows (control chars/U+2028/U+2029/C0 seps in content, arbitrary JSON-safe properties, includeProperties both ways): line count == block count; no id-less forged-bullet line; collapse idempotent. Note the agent-cli test gotcha: protocol resolves to dist in vitest — compile the package first the way its existing tests do.
